{"id": "11th_tamil_u3_q140", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_3", "lesson_id": "grammar_pagupatham", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "pyq_pagupatham_essential", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "[TNPSC] ஒரு பகுபதத்தில் இன்றியமையாமல் இடம்பெற வேண்டிய இரு முதன்மை உறுப்புகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "சந்தி, சாரியை", "B": "சாரியை, விகாரம்", "C": "இடைநிலை, சந்தி", "D": "பகுதி, விகுதி (அடிச்சொல்லும் இறுதி உறுப்பும்)"}, "explanation": "எல்லாப் பகுபதங்களிலும் பகுதியும் விகுதியும் கட்டாயமாக இடம்பெறும்; பிற உறுப்புகள் சொல்லின் தேவைக்கேற்ப வரும்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "[TNPSC] Which two foundational components are indispensably mandatory in every divisible word (Pagupatham)?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Sandhi and Saariyai", "B": "Saariyai and Vikaram", "C": "Infix and Sandhi", "D": "Paguthi and Vikuthi (Root base and terminal suffix)"}, "explanation": "Paguthi (root) and Vikuthi (suffix) are the two indispensable structural pillars of a Pagupatham."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 54, "chapter": null, "section":